ency in index space. A representation with dense edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indices also reports ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeIndexBound"},{"text":", and then ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeIndex(of:)"},{"text":" maps edge positions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one-to-one onto ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<edgeIndexBound"},{"text":" (Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edge_index"},{"text":", petgraph’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EdgeIndexable"},{"text":"), so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithms that mark edges (bridges, cut vertices, Euler tours) keep that state in arrays too.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdgeIndices(ofIndex:)"},{"text":" lists them parallel to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Laws."}]},{"text":" Every conformer satisfies:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexCount == vertices.count"},{"type":"text","text":", the vertices are distinct, and every edge’s endpoints are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeCount == edges.count"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For every vertex ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists the position of each edge with an end at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" once per end (a self-loop twice); each such edge has ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as an endpoint;",